# Portability constraints

- Target ANSI C89 / ISO C90 compatibility.
- Keep DOS/OpenWatcom and GCC compatibility in mind when changing headers, types, or libc usage.
- Avoid compiler extensions, platform-specific assumptions, and C99/C11 features unless already established in the codebase.
- Prefer explicit ownership, fixed-size arrays, and static storage over dynamic allocation.
- Keep platform-specific behaviour isolated to platform/render layers.
